><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3916180/extras/0a87cdb5652921754bdda5f067b15c19.webm?t=1763281716\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3916180/extras/0a87cdb5652921754bdda5f067b15c19.mp4?t=1763281716\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&lt;Transport Legion&gt; Is:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A turn-based game for deliberate planners (pause anytime, no rush).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >About adapting, not memorizing solutions</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A bit challenging, similar to a German-style board game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >1-2 hour sessions with no meta-progression grind.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A game with conservative numerical values, small yet precise</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Not Included:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No real-time reflexes or twitch gameplay.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No rigid best build—every run demands innovation.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No A game that can be cleared without thinking.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No repetitive grinding or meta-progression.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No endless number-chasing; just polished, meaningful choices.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game was developed by a solo developer. To make the game accessible to more players worldwide, the localization has been assisted by AI.</p>",
